The guppy sequence is NOT a particle effect.

It is a choreographed cinematic formation reveal inspired by the “fanned deck” motion language from the reference — except translated into living marine motion.

The school of guppies should feel:

* intelligent
* synchronized
* elegant
* atmospheric
* orchestrated
* dimensional
* cinematic

The effect should feel like:
a hidden underwater swarm assembling itself into formation around the koi.

====================================================
CORE VISUAL IDEA

The guppies behave like a diagonal “living deck”.

Imagine:

* cards snapping into a staggered diagonal stack
    BUT
* expressed as living fish moving through volumetric depth.

The formation should:

* emerge from deep background space
* travel along a shared diagonal vector
* settle behind the koi
* hold briefly
* dissolve back into the abyss

This is NOT:

* random flocking
* aquarium simulation
* generic boids demo

It is:
precisely art-directed cinematic choreography.

====================================================
FORMATION DESIGN

The school forms along a diagonal receding axis.

Visual arrangement:
foreground lower-left → background upper-right
(or inverse depending on composition)

Each guppy occupies:

* slightly different depth
* slightly different rotation
* slightly different scale
* slight spacing irregularity

The formation should resemble:

* layered silhouettes
* stacked glass cards
* receding perspective planes

The school must visually frame the koi hero.

====================================================
ENTRANCE CHOREOGRAPHY

MOST IMPORTANT SECTION.

The guppies DO NOT spawn visibly.

Each guppy should:

1. begin deep in fog
2. extremely small silhouette
3. low opacity
4. faint emissive edge
5. travel rapidly but smoothly along diagonal vector
6. decelerate elegantly into slot
7. settle with slight overshoot drift

The feeling should resemble:
luxury UI cards snapping into place
translated into living underwater creatures.

====================================================
TIMING SYSTEM

Use staggered choreography.

DO NOT animate all guppies simultaneously.

Instead:

* each fish enters with delayed offset
* 60–140ms stagger range
* cascading wave timing
* rhythmic assembly feel

The sequence should feel:

* musical
* orchestrated
* satisfying

NOT:

* mechanical
* mathematically uniform

====================================================
MOTION CHARACTER

Movement style:

* smooth spline interpolation
* curved travel arcs
* soft easing
* underwater inertia
* subtle drag

Each guppy should:

* tilt while accelerating
* level while locking into formation
* drift microscopically after arrival

NO:

* linear interpolation
* robotic straight-line movement
* instant stopping

====================================================
FORMATION LOCK-IN MOMENT

After all guppies arrive:

* formation stabilizes briefly
* motion slows almost to stillness
* koi slowly rotates toward camera
* lighting intensifies subtly
* bloom edges peak softly
* headline text reveals

This is the emotional “hero lock” moment.

Hold duration:
~1.5–2.5 seconds

The audience should subconsciously think:
“Everything aligned.”

====================================================
KOI RELATIONSHIP

The guppies must reinforce the koi’s importance.

The school should:

* orbit compositionally around koi
* point visual attention toward koi
* enhance depth behind koi
* never overpower koi visually

The koi remains:
the king of the frame.

====================================================
DEPTH & PARALLAX

Critical.

Every guppy must exist at different Z-depths.

Implement:

* layered depth offsets
* subtle parallax
* different fog intensities
* varying blur softness
* perspective scaling

Foreground guppies:

* larger
* sharper
* brighter rim light

Background guppies:

* faded
* smaller
* swallowed partially by haze

This depth layering is ESSENTIAL.

====================================================
LIGHTING

Each guppy should catch:

* thin rim lighting
* bloom streaks
* reflective highlights
* underwater caustic flickers

Lighting behavior:

* emissive edge pulses slightly during arrival
* brightness settles after lock-in

Avoid:

* neon overload
* glowing cartoon fish
* equal brightness everywhere

====================================================
BLOOM TRAILS

During fast arrival movement:

* subtle bloom streak trails appear
* very restrained
* dissolve quickly

Think:
luxury motion graphics
NOT:
anime speed lines.

The trails should:

* enhance velocity perception
* reinforce cinematic polish
* disappear after formation settles

====================================================
FORMATION DRIFT

Once assembled:
the school should drift together microscopically.

Like:
a suspended underwater constellation.

Implement:

* collective slow sway
* subtle oscillation
* minute spacing shifts
* synchronized breathing motion

The school should feel alive even while stationary.

====================================================
DISSOLVE EXIT

As scroll progresses:
the formation should collapse elegantly.

NOT:
instant disappearance.

Instead:

* guppies peel away gradually
* dissolve into fog depth
* spacing increases
* opacity fades
* diagonal structure breaks apart

Some guppies:

* dive deeper
* rotate away
* vanish into darkness

The koi remains longest before transitioning.

====================================================
CAMERA CHOREOGRAPHY

During formation:

* camera subtly dollies
* slight lateral drift
* gentle push-in
* eased buoyancy motion

The camera movement must:
support the formation reveal,
not distract from it.

====================================================
